OL,1,V7w3s7s35                          G4/9
OL,2,V55555555CLABOUR PONDERS
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CDEBATE ON PICKETS
OL,4,Q
OL,5, Labour leaders meet at Westminster
OL,6, today to decide whether to press for
OL,7, an emergency Commons debate on police
OL,8, handling of the miners' pickets.
OL,9,Q
OL,10, The Speaker has indicated he would
OL,11, probably agree to such a request. If
OL,12, Labour does get the debate, it will
OL,13, take place tomorrow.
OL,14,Q
OL,15,SGThe NUR executive is to meet today
OL,16, over a group of rail guards refusing to
OL,17, black the movement of coal.
OL,18,Q
OL,19, The 75 men at Shirebrook Depot in Notts
OL,20, handle 40 trains a day - about half the
OL,21, Nottinghamshire coalfield's output.
OL,23,F]DFrom 09-04-84 / teletextarchive.com
