OL,2,V55555555CHOUSTON DELAYS
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CSATELLITE RESCUE
OL,5, American astronauts have put back their
OL,6, bid to retrieve a disabled satellite
OL,7, until tomorrow.
OL,9, And instead of crewman George Nelson
OL,10, using a jet backpack to capture the
OL,11, Solar Max it is hoped to use the
OL,12, shuttle's mechanical arm.
OL,14, The satellite is wobbling and when
OL,15, Nelson tried to retrieve it to bring
OL,16, it back to the shuttle for repairs
OL,17, his docking mechanism failed.
OL,19, Houston plans to manoeuvre the shuttle
OL,20, to within 50ft of the 2.5-ton craft and
OL,21, use a robot arm to pluck it from space.
OL,23,F]DFrom 09-04-84 / teletextarchive.com
