OL,2,V55555555CIRA KILLERS 'IN CHURCH
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CWITH VICTIM'
OL,4,Q
OL,5, Police believe the IRA gunmen who shot
OL,6, a Belfast JP as he made his way home
OL,7, from Mass were in the congregation at
OL,8, the church.
OL,9,Q
OL,10, Catholic magistrate Tom Travers is
OL,11, fighting for his life in hospital after
OL,12, having six bullets removed from his
OL,13, body in two operations.
OL,14,Q
OL,15, Mr Travers' daughter, Mary, was killed
OL,16, in the ambush at St Bridget's Church.
OL,17,Q
OL,18, Police believe the killers sat just a
OL,19, few pews from the family during the
OL,20, service and kept loaded handguns hidden
OL,21, in their clothing.
OL,23,F]DFrom 09-04-84 / teletextarchive.com
