OL,2,V55555555CJAILED TISDALL
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CIN APPEAL BID
OL,5, Jailed Foreign Office clerk Sarah
OL,6, Tisdall was appearing in court in
OL,7, London today to appeal against her six-
OL,8, month jail sentence on a secrets charge
OL,10, The expedited Appeal Court hearing
OL,11, comes only 17 days after she was jailed
OL,12, at the Old Bailey for leaking documents
OL,13, about Cruise missiles to the Guardian.
OL,15, Counsel for Miss Tisdall, 23, was first
OL,16, applying for leave to appeal.
OL,18, The judges would go on immediately to
OL,19, hear her substantative appeal and
OL,20, review her sentence if the first
OL,21, application was granted.
OL,23,F]DFrom 09-04-84 / teletextarchive.com
